From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: weizxfree <weizhangxiang2022@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 21:40:05 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] feat(web): an embedded run that shows nothing outside its
 pages

For an editor served to a host page (KnowWork):
- --web-only / GENOFFICE_WEB_ONLY=1 runs the web server only: no window, no
  dock icon, no update checks
- a native dialog no browser tab asked for is answered "cancel" and logged
- window.alert shows as the page's toast
- a page framed by its host tells the host when the connection drops, and
  reloads when the server closes its document
- a page framed by its host tells the host each time its file is written
  (Save, AutoSave, an agent's save), so the host can keep its copy current
- a page framed by its host keeps file dialogs on the user's computer: a save
  downloads the written file, an open uses the browser's file picker and uploads
  the chosen files; the server's disk is never browsed
- an open-folder dialog in such a page is an export target (Export as Images,
  mail merge into files): one written file downloads as it is, several as a zip
- a web-only run never reveals or opens a file on its own machine
